  text-align: right;
  white-space: pre-wrap;
}
</style>
<small>shape: (3, 8)</small><table border="1" class="dataframe"><thead><tr><th>year</th><th>time_hour</th><th>origin</th><th>dest</th><th>tailnum</th><th>carrier</th><th>year_built</th><th>type</th></tr><tr><td>i64</td><td>datetime[μs, America/New_York]</td><td>str</td><td>str</td><td>str</td><td>str</td><td>i64</td><td>str</td></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>2013</td><td>2013-01-01 05:00:00 EST</td><td>&quot;EWR&quot;</td><td>&quot;IAH&quot;</td><td>&quot;N14228&quot;</td><td>&quot;UA&quot;</td><td>1999</td><td>&quot;Fixed wing multi engine&quot;</td></tr><tr><td>2013</td><td>2013-01-01 05:00:00 EST</td><td>&quot;LGA&quot;</td><td>&quot;IAH&quot;</td><td>&quot;N24211&quot;</td><td>&quot;UA&quot;</td><td>1998</td><td>&quot;Fixed wing multi engine&quot;</td></tr><tr><td>2013</td><td>2013-01-01 05:00:00 EST</td><td>&quot;JFK&quot;</td><td>&quot;MIA&quot;</td><td>&quot;N619AA&quot;</td><td>&quot;AA&quot;</td><td>1990</td><td>&quot;Fixed wing multi engine&quot;</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
```
:::
:::


**Different key names.** `left_on="dest", right_on="faa"` ≈
`join_by(dest == faa)`. The output keeps `dest` and drops `faa`.
`coalesce=False` keeps both (≈ `keep = TRUE`).

**Compound keys.** Pass a list. `time_hour` is `Datetime("us",
"America/New_York")` in both tables, and it has to be: the unit and the zone
must match (@sec-join-dtypes):

::: {#abf35e70 .cell execution_count=9}
``` {.python .cell-code}
flights_weather_df = flights2_df.join(
    weather_df.select("origin", "time_hour", "temp", "wind_speed"),
    on=["origin", "time_hour"], how="left", maintain_order="left",
)
flights_weather_df.head(3)
```

::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=9}
